<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virginia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Virginia is a region on the Atlantic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, named in honour of Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>. The colony founded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a> in 1607 was the first permanent English settlement in America. Its tobacco plantations, worked increasingly by enslaved Africans, made it a central part of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> in the Atlantic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virginia.jpg" alt="Virginia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LadyofHats with additional editing by 痛 and Patrickneil / Charles Keck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Virginia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The first permanent English settlement in the Americas came at Jamestown, <b>Virginia</b>, in 1607, a colony so precarious that the great majority of its settlers died during the “Starving Time” of 1609–1610.</blockquote><a href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Lincoln's call for 75,000 militia followed on 15 April, and <b>Virginia</b>, Arkansas, Tennessee and North Carolina seceded between April and May.</blockquote><a href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>From the late sixteenth century overseas trade expanded through chartered companies such as the East India Company, founded in 1600, and through colonies in North America and the Caribbean, beginning with Jamestown in <b>Virginia</b> in 1607.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Overseas commerce grew rapidly under the Navigation Acts, which reserved colonial trade for British ships: sugar from Jamaica and Barbados, tobacco from <b>Virginia</b> and Maryland and textiles from India were re-exported across Europe, and Glasgow prospered on tobacco after the union.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The ‘20. and odd’ Africans landed in English <b>Virginia</b> in August 1619 were probably captives from Portuguese campaigns against Ndongo, shipped from Luanda on a slave ship bound for Veracruz.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-ndongo">Kingdom of Ndongo · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Joseph Jenkins Roberts, a merchant born in <b>Virginia</b>, became the first president.</blockquote><a href="/empire/liberia">Liberia · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
